@startuml cpp_standard_features
title MicroLA C++ Standard Feature Progression

skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "C++20 (Baseline - Required)" <<Rectangle>> #E6FFE6 {
    component "Core C++20 Features" as cpp20
    note right of cpp20
        • Concepts:
          - Arithmetic<T>
          - FloatingPoint<T>
          - Integral<T>
        • if constexpr / constexpr loops
        • inline variables
        • MICROLA_BIT_CAST (std::bit_cast)
        • consteval (MICROLA_CONSTEVAL)

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Concepts defined in umbrella;
        not constraints on every core template
        Branch optimization
        Safe type punning
        Compile-time validation
        (stack-size config check)
    end note
}

package "C++23 Enhancements" <<Rectangle>> #FFE6F3 {
    component "MICROLA_IF_CONSTEVAL" as cpp23
    note right of cpp23
        • if consteval (MICROLA_IF_CONSTEVAL)

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Feature-test guarded if consteval
        Fallback is if(false)
    end note
}

package "C++26 (Conditional Library Support)" <<Rectangle>> #F0E6FF {
    component "MICROLA_CONSTEXPR_TRIG" as cpp26
    note right of cpp26
        • constexpr math functions:
          - std::sin, std::cos
          - std::sqrt, std::atan2

        **MicroLA Usage:**
        Selected trig methods become constexpr
        only with an implementing standard library.
        C++20/23 fixed rotations use explicit coefficients.

        **Example:**
        constexpr auto rot =
          Mat<float,2,2>::rotation(0.785398f);
    end note
}

cpp20 -down-> cpp23 : Adds
cpp23 -down-> cpp26 : Adds

note as FeatureDetection
    **Automatic Feature Detection:**

        C++20 is the required baseline.
        Optional features prefer feature-test macros:
        __cpp_concepts
        __cpp_consteval
        __cpp_if_consteval
        __cpp_lib_bit_cast

    MICROLA_CONSTEXPR_TRIG currently checks
    __cplusplus >= 202600L.
    Actual math constant evaluation also requires
    standard-library support; compile the expression.
end note

@enduml

